## API Endpoints Tested

All endpoints return valid JSON matching the frontend contract:

| Endpoint | Status | Sample Response |
|---|---|---|
| `GET /api/health` | ✅ 200 | `{ "status": "ok", "uptime_seconds": 160.5, "last_mission_timestamp": "...", "log_size_mb": 0.08 }` |
| `GET /api/mission/state` | ✅ 200 | `{ "state": "ready", "progress": 1.0, "message": "Mission SIM_... ready." }` |
| `GET /api/mission/list` | ✅ 200 | `[{ "id": "SIM_...", "label": "Flight SIM_...", "timestamp": "..." }]` |
| `GET /api/mission/latest` | ✅ 200 | Full mission JSON with `mission`, `battery`, `gps`, `profile`, `health`, `payload` |
| `GET /api/downloads/meta` | ✅ 200 | `{ "raw_log_mb": null, "json_mb": 0.08 }` |
| `GET /api/downloads/raw-log` | ✅ ready | FileResponse (no .BIN in simulation mode) |
| `GET /api/downloads/processed-json` | ✅ ready | FileResponse of mission JSON |
| `GET /payload/*` | ✅ ready | Static file serving from `storage/payload/` |

## Simulation Mode Verification

The worker successfully cycled through all lifecycle states:

```
idle → downloading (with 0–100% progress) → parsing → ready
```

Server startup log confirmed the full cycle in ~9 seconds.

## How to Run

### Development (Simulation Mode)
```bash
cd UAV-backend
pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000
```

### Live Mode (Pixhawk Connected)
```bash
set MAVLINK_CONNECTION=com3        # or udp:127.0.0.1:14550
python -m uvicorn main:app --port 8000
```

### Frontend Integration
The dashboard's Vite dev server can proxy to the backend. The backend serves on port 8000, and the frontend already uses `/api` prefix which can be configured in `vite.config.js`:

```js
export default defineConfig({
  server: {
    proxy: {
      '/api': 'http://localhost:8000',
      '/payload': 'http://localhost:8000',
    }
  }
});
```
